  "offlinePermissionsTitle": "Permission purposes at a glance",
  "offlinePermissionPurposes": "Nearby devices: scan BLE peripherals, query system connections, connect to a selected device and read or subscribe to characteristics. Peripheral names, addresses, signal and service information support local demos.\nLocation on older Android: needed only for BLE scanning on Android 11 and earlier, without location tracking.\nNotifications: requested when you tap the authorization button, for local test notifications you post. Cancel them in the demo or system notification area.\nBiometrics: verified by the system when you start authentication. The app cannot read fingerprint or face templates or lock-screen passwords.\nFiles and fonts: only items you select in the system picker are processed.\nOrdinary media permissions: network-state and wake-lock declarations come from media components. This offline APK still has no INTERNET permission.\nDeclining optional access affects only the related operation. Agreeing to the privacy notice does not grant these permissions. The Bluetooth component caches peripheral addresses and service UUIDs locally; leaving the module or revoking permission does not erase the cache. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes local copies along with other local data. See the full policy above for permission names, retention and component details."
